OL,3,GNEWSAInside the Tudor house sold by
OL,4,Acouncil for #10k
OL,5,
OL,6,FOne of the oldest houses in Plymouth
OL,7,Fhas been sold by the city council for
OL,8,Fjust #10,000 in the hope it is
OL,9,Frestored.
OL,11,FDescribed as a "precious historic
OL,12,Fproperty", the 16th Century Merchant's
OL,13,FHouse was first recorded as being owned
OL,14,Fby Capt William Parker, a friend of
OL,15,Fsailor and navigator Sir Francis Drake.
OL,17,FIt was sold to amateur historian and
OL,18,Fproperty developer Joe Radmore who said
OL,19,Fhe planned to renovate the property so
OL,20,Ftourists could stay in it and feel what
OL,21,Fit was like to live there.
OL,23,APub: 05-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,346,340,200,160,0,100
